((date 2026-11-14) (slug price-band-binding)
 (hypothesis
  "Price-band binding diagnostic (pre-registered in dev/experiments/price-band-binding-2026-11-13/README.md at c0991e023, #3597; read #3602): one S cell (#3595's pb-S-k0 spec: record config, Seeded tie order seed 0, top-3000 PIT v12 deduped yearly lists, 2000-01-01 -> 2026-06-26) run with --emit-candidates; every screened date's long top-20 pool re-ranked offline under Price_band_seeded (edges [8;14;33], band from the decision-date raw close). L1 = share of binding dates whose top-20 set changes; L2 = E_net = expected net >= +100 % trades the re-drawn funded tickets buy at #3595's per-band S rates; T = monster-rate ratio and mean capped ride of the names swapped in vs out; plus the breakout sub-gate that first drops cheap (< $14) monsters. Rule 1 in order: CLOSE-AXIS if L2 < 0.75; PARK if L1 < 0.25; CLOSE-AXIS if T has >= 20 monsters and ratio < 1.0 or the in mean ride is not above the out mean ride; FRESH if L1 >= 0.25, L2 >= 1.5 and T passes; else PARK; not applied if the band proxy agrees on < 90 % of placed tickets. Rule 2: UNDERPOWERED below 30 cheap monsters per view; DIAL-STUDY on a gate with share >= 20 % and lift >= 1.25 in both views; else NO CONCLUSION (one view / immaterial) or NOTHING.")
 (base_scenario
  "price-band-binding-2026-11-13: one cell pbb-S-k0-s0 at HEAD 645065bb2, image sha256:3865e48e8a61, warehouse v12wk-9236 + corpact-2026-10-27 + bars data-20261102, Claude cloud; every per-arm artifact byte-identical to #3595 pb-S-k0 (trades.csv md5 0928cfe4, +1,472.76 %, max DD 27.22 %, Sharpe 0.634, 576 trades); SC1/SC2 PASS on all 1,099 longs-open dates (Alphabetical control misses 877); band proxy 621/644 = 96.4 % (621/683 = 90.9 % counting the 39 tickets without a bar); single cell, no V6 pair (V6 INV PASS)")
 (window_id top3000-pitv12dedup-1999-2025-26y-k0-emitcand)
 (baseline_label pbb-S-k0)
 (variants
  (((label P-offline-rerank-k0) (config_hash price-band-seeded-offline-k0@645065bb2) (aggregate ()))))
 (verdict Reject)
 (notes
  "CLOSE-AXIS by Rule 1 branch 3 (read/rules.txt; README order and bars): L2 E_net 0.953 >= 0.75, L1 0.690 >= 0.25, then T: 205 monsters, ratio 3.07 (in > out in both halves), but the swapped-in mean capped ride +4.0 % is not above the swapped-out +4.1 % (diff -0.0010). Rule 2: NO CONCLUSION (immaterial): Breakout_volume window-view lift 3.27 rests on 2 cheap monster events (0.5 % share); Stage_setup first-drops 44.7 % (exact) / 32.0 % (window) of cheap monsters with a row at lift 0.99 / 0.88. CLASS: REJECT-as-default-but-legitimate-axis (keep-as-axis): Price_band_seeded stays default-off; not do-not-revive, not retirement-eligible; a one-path proxy read rejects prioritising the axis, not the mechanism; no new pre-registration follows; no default changes. CALIBRATION: the ride clause read a zero (inside one SE of roughly 0.6-1.0 pp; +0.3 pp under convention F, +0.2 pp in 2013-26, paired per date mean +0.9 / median -1.4 pp, 46.8 % positive), and a read defect touches it: fwd.awk classes 2025-26 swaps the store truncates as delisted (STORE_END 2026-09-11 is the latest bar of an uneven store; 33 in / 34 out deduped rows after 2025-09-12, only 2 classed T), so CLOSE-AXIS vs PARK is not robust; FRESH is out of reach either way (L2 < 1.5) and both outcomes spend no cells. WHY: the cut falls inside a score tie on 83.8 % of open dates and the order changes the top 20 on 69 % (1,744 swaps each way; 91 % of the names cut >= $33, every name promoted < $33). Promoted names double 3x as often but win less often (38.5 vs 42.0 %) with a deeper left tail (p10 -17.3 vs -12.3 %), so the capped 30-week-WMA ride ties. 94.7 % of S's top-20 slots never fund (No_structural_stop dominates; fundable share 3.0 / 4.2 / 5.2 / 5.8 % from < $8 to >= $33), so the swaps re-draw 84 funded tickets in 26 y (30 % under $14), worth E_net 0.953 +/- 0.31 (Poisson on r(b); 3/2/4/5 distinct doublers by band; 0.920 with ADSK 2003 in its decision band) = about 0.10-0.18 log, under the 0.2 log floor and 30-50 % of #3595's +0.348. #3595's gap = that expectation plus one shared draw: the cut swaps P-k0 placed (43, worth 1.14 expected doublers) delivered MERC 2010-11-12 (S rank 25: #3595's unresolved channel was the cut) and ADMA 2023-08-18 (S rank 22); on S's path the order would also cut LGND 2012-12-14 (+233 %), which P-k0 kept by path. FORWARD: no further ordering/tiebreak lever or band-edge sweep on price; the trait's binding gates are Stage_setup (breadth, no lift), the top-N slot and post-cut fundability, all already probed (floor-nearest NOT LIVE, top-N 40 not promotable). #3598 (C1 2013-26, C2 top-1000) is read on its own rule; an ESCALATE there meets this CLOSE-AXIS and goes to the user. Writeup: dev/experiments/price-band-binding-2026-11-13/README.md Results."))
